KG42.register("slice-clusters-a0040c1fc9491c71e3c09a0f",{"id":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v142-d-K003","paper":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets","title":"Constrained contract selection, bilateral price adjustment and day-ahead allocation pricing","source_pointer":"/clusters/84","node_ids":["COMP-75186ff50e007d27","COMP-10be07664c6496b7","COMP-535650ecb2e046e9","COMP-b249861ac893186a","COMP-486b93e7e3eb4336"],"rule_refs":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R002","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R003","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R006","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R005","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R004"],"visible_rule_refs":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R002","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R003","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R006","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R005","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R004"],"suppressed_rule_refs":[],"edges":[{"global_edge_id":"S-c975694be911d5f1","source":"COMP-10be07664c6496b7","target":"COMP-75186ff50e007d27","type":"links","assertion_ids":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001"],"rule_refs":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R002"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-1b272357ba647227","source":"COMP-75186ff50e007d27","target":"COMP-10be07664c6496b7","type":"links","assertion_ids":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E001"],"rule_refs":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R003"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-bddcca51aa21463d","source":"COMP-10be07664c6496b7","target":"COMP-535650ecb2e046e9","type":"links","assertion_ids":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R006::E::v141-c-R006-E001"],"rule_refs":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R006"],"internal":false}],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"interface_annotations":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta-Pf-it","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E25"],"rationale":"The source explicitly brings the pre-entry retail resource plan into the flexibility market. This plan can be optimized in prior scheduling and serves as a fixed input in R002; this interface does not merge the local roles of the two stages."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g02-e21"],"rationale":"The source places potential contracts between tradable entity pairs and determines potential transactions and initializes prices at the start of bargaining. Permissions therefore delimit the negotiation counterparties, but C does not explicitly give a construction formula from permissions to the transaction set."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X002","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta-Xi","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22"],"rationale":"Each round's bids are used to construct the upstream and downstream contracts selectable by agents, which are then selected according to individual utility. This is an interface from bids to selection input, not an identity mapping between price quantities and contract sets."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x-Xprime-i","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X005","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X006","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"The supplied excerpt divides selection results into upstream and downstream contracts and then identifies transactions selected by buyers but not selected by sellers. The overall selection, side-specific selections and excess-demand set have different roles and cannot be directly declared to be the same quantity."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x-Xprime","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"The excerpt interprets the aggregation of upstream selections at stopping as the market result and explains stability under fully substitutable preferences. This source supports functional linkage, but C has not yet expressed the complete mapping from terminal selections to the global result."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e25"],"rationale":"The DSO continuously raises bids for unrealized and necessary contracts, which links to the terminal allocation satisfying the demand boundary; this result is explicitly conditional on sufficient prosumer flexibility and cannot be generalized into an unconditional feasibility guarantee."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L008","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x001","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"The two chains respectively reference the buyer and seller bid states of the same mechanism in the update and pricing interpretations. Bid sides always remain separate; equality of the two sides' prices is not inferred from the stopping condition."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L009","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"],"rationale":"The two records express the restriction, within the same result set, that each transaction corresponds to at most one contract; the pricing chain emphasizes its unique-price meaning and does not constitute an additional independent rule."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L010","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"Both reference the same stopping condition of no price change, but R003 records completion determination, while R006 also claims that an agreed price is reached. Retain the different expressions; do not treat the stopping predicate as a complete proof of price consistency."}],"annotation_policy":"Original D connections are annotations, not additional S edges.","empty_after_chain_suppression":false});
